                <pb facs="0803" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/33770: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-03T18:00:00-04:00">April 3, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1117. We fully approve of your action reported in your 2020, April 1, and we have
                    sent you in clear today the text of my statement to the press<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d735-f1"/> expressing the deep regret of all of us over this tragic
                    incident as well as Ambassador Winant’s report of his and General Spaatz’s call
                    on the Swiss Chargé in London to express similar sentiments. Assistant Secretary
                    Long and the Director of the Office of European Affairs, Mr. Dunn representing
                    me, called on the Swiss Minister this afternoon to express in person the regret
                    of this Government over the incident and to inform the Minister that an
                    investigation was under way by the military authorities and as soon as it was
                    completed the findings would be made available to the Minister.</p>
                <p>We hope the foregoing will be of some use to you in your conversations with Swiss
                    officials. If you have occasion to discuss the matter further with Mr.
                    Pilet-Golaz please express our deep appreciation for his orders that press and
                    radio announcements in Switzerland should be restrained and factual.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
